\section{JIRF Scenarios and Bootstrap Procedure}\label{apx:stddev}
We explore three main shock scenarios to generate our JIRF analyses. We shock all piglet, all hog, and all pork province prices by one standard deviation. The standard deviation is calculated by province over the \textit{Pre} period. Thus, if the $i$th province price is one of the shocked variables, the magnitude of the shock is one standard deviation 
