Each experiment is run for $50$ trials to ensure the reliability of the results, and the average CPU time is computed. Let \( t_q^r \) and \( t_c^r \) represent the average CPU times required for computing \( X_q^r \) and \( X_c^r \), respectively. Similarly, let \( t_q^l \) and \( t_c^l \) represent the average CPU times  required for computing \( X_q^l \) and \( X_c^l \), respectively.

