    \caption{\textbf{Visualization of the stochastic model.} Particle populations observed at the snapshot instant ($t = 0$) have long histories that cannot be observed. Here, particles are ``born'' at a rate $\lambda$ (yellow circles) in the source location $z$ (yellow line). The particles diffuse until  they are either degraded (green circles) or exit the domain (pink circles). The faded trajectories are for particles that left the system before time zero, while the purple trajectories are those that remain active and are observed in the $t=0$ snapshot. Nondimensional $x,t$ shown with rates $\lambda=10$, $\mu=1.5$ corresponding original simulation parameters $\ksource=5, \kswitch=0.75, D=0.5, L=3,$ $L_0=1, z=1$.    }\label{fig:snapshot-roots}
