\section{Empirical findings}\label{sec:empirical_findings}

In this section we present our empirical results. We first investigate in Section \ref{sec:swap_pricing_fit} the accuracy of the swap pricing model (\ref{eq:swap_value}) relative to the values reported in EMIR. We consider the pricing error not only in the contract values but also in their time-series changes, as a small error in the latter is what matters most in sensitivity analysis. In Section \ref{sec:sensitivity} we discuss the estimates of banks' interest rate risk exposures, which allow to determine if and how effectively banks use swaps to hedge risk of their fixed-rate bonds.
