In the above,  $A_1^{+}=\al_2^{(1)}/(\sigma_1|\al_2^{(1)}|^2+\sigma_2\chi|\al_2^{(2)}|^2)^{1/2}$, $A_2^{+}=\al_2^{(1)}/(\sigma_1|\al_2^{(1)}|^2\chi^{-1}+\sigma_2|\al_2^{(2)}|^2)^{1/2}$,\\ $\chi=(|k_2-l_1|^2|k_1+k_2^*|^2|k_2+l_1|^2|k_1-k_2^*|^2)/(|k_1-k_2|^2|k_2+l_1^*|^2|k_1+k_2|^2|k_2-l_1^*|^2)$, $\phi^+=\frac{1}{2}\ln\frac{|k_1-k_2|^2|k_2-l_1|^2\Lam_3}{2i(k_2-k_2^*)(k_2+k_2*)^2|k_1-k_2^*|^2|k_1+k_2^*|^4|k_2-l_1^*|^2|k_2+l_1^*|^4}$, where $\Lambda_3$ is defined in Appendix B. Here, $l$ in $A_l^{+}$, $l=1,2$, refers to the SW components  and the superscript ($+$) denotes after collision.

