Lastly, Figure~\ref{fig3} depicts the equilibrium annuity price process for increasing or decreasing $\beta_{\Sigma}(j)$ with respect to $j$. We observe that if $\beta_{\Sigma}(j)$ decreases (or increases, respectively) in $j$, the annuity price $A(j)$ is higher (or lower, respectively) than $1/\beta_{\Sigma}(j)$.




