\begin{lem}\label{le:inv}
The operator $\MM = \mathcal{M}(r',s',f',g';q)$ \eqref{eq:M} satisfies the following inversion relations of two types:
\begin{itemize}
\item[(I)] Ordinary type: $\mathcal{M}(s',r',f',q^{-1}f';q) \mathcal{M}(s',r',f',q^{-1}f';q) = r' s' \cdot \mathrm{Id}$.
\begin{align}\label{M-I}
